# Node.js / TypeScript

When editing matching files:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Prefer the project's TypeScript/JavaScript skill; if none, load this plugin's `skills/ankyr-nodejs/SKILL.md` if installed.
- Load its `references/` only when the skill directs (including `references/npm-tooling.md` when deps, lockfile, lint scripts, or audit come up).
- Follow the nearest `AGENT.md` chain for Validate commands and type-alias conventions.

Key rules: no `any`, no `@ts-nocheck`, async/await only, no empty bound catch, only `console.error/warn`, prefer canonical/`@types/*` types over workarounds.
